1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,938
WenQuest virtual labs run in the browser: nothing to install,

2
00:00:03,958 --> 00:00:05,129
and nothing to break.

3
00:00:06,149 --> 00:00:07,660
Inverted pendulum PID control,

4
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:10,417
with the dynamics checked step by step against MuJoCo.

5
00:00:10,887 --> 00:00:14,764
Tune the gains and watch the angle, cart position and force curves,

6
00:00:15,234 --> 00:00:19,701
while the AI lab assistant reads your runs and points the way without giving

7
00:00:19,721 --> 00:00:20,351
the answer.

8
00:00:21,371 --> 00:00:24,812
A two-link arm: kinematics, trajectory planning and control,

9
00:00:24,832 --> 00:00:26,888
from equations to an arm that moves.

10
00:00:27,908 --> 00:00:32,212
For university physics, the kinematics bench gives every concept a scene:

11
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:35,174
frames, projectiles, circular and relative motion,

12
00:00:35,644 --> 00:00:38,302
and every scene comes with a robotics problem.

13
00:00:39,321 --> 00:00:43,830
The PLC bench wires a web PLC to a 3D machine. Write the program, run it,

14
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:45,195
step through the scan,

15
00:00:45,665 --> 00:00:50,372
and inject jams, broken wires or motor overloads to practise troubleshooting.

16
00:00:51,392 --> 00:00:55,873
Microelectronics: size the transistors and see delay and power at once,

17
00:00:56,343 --> 00:00:59,950
then go on to Verilog synthesis and layout, from RTL all the way to GDS.

18
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:03,331
Every lab comes with a guide and a report template,

19
00:01:03,351 --> 00:01:05,992
and there are cloud GPU labs that run CUDA in JupyterLab.
